david_ari_9@hotmail.com wrote:
>
> I am a level 15 orcish rouge (which is now my favorite class. Throwing
> 4 daggers in 1 round is great) I'm on dungeon level 14, and I know
> that the vibrating square is on dungeon level 15, but I haven't
> explored the floor yet. My max HP is 109, max power is 52.

I have read the other post saying this is the Quest portal not the VS.

Generally daggers rule for multifire missile combat but they do not rule
for melee combat.  The right tool for the job.

> I have Grimtooth (unenchanted at the moment, but I do have enchant
> weapon scrolls identified and will get it enchanted once I find a
> magic marker)

Grimtooth does not stack therefore it is a poor missile combat dagger. 
Go for other melee weapons.

> and 11 +6 blessed orcish daggers, as well as 15 blessed
> regular daggers as backup.

Over time build up a stack of a dozen or so elven daggers, then highly
enchant the stack and switch to it.  No hurry doing so but the quality
of daggers for damage goes orcish < regular < elven all with the same
weight.  Until you get the elven stack to +6 stay with the orcish ones.

> I also was incredibly lucky with a wand of polymorph and managed to
> change my pet dog into a lich, which has sense become a level 26 arch-
> lich with invisibility, 201 HP, and a -16 AC

Others have mentioned the problems with a lich pet and wielding Stormy.
Having gotten Stormy as a gift your broadsword skill slot is open.  I
suggest using one of your many elven broadswords until you are offered
to enhance it.  The advantage is it's not an artifact that automatically
attacks.  Then drop it into your stash and have Stormy available for
heavy melee.

> Bag of holding from Sohkoban (has been blessed with holy water)

This allows you to carry a lot more item.  It also allows you to be less
selective about what to carry.  That's arguably a good thing the few few
ascensions.

> Copious numbers of offensive wands, plus a few wands of digging,
> teleportation, polymorph, create monster, enlightenment, and a few
> unidentified ones
> Lockpick
> Magic whistle
> Uncursed unicorn horn
> towel
> stethoscope
> Flute which I'm pretty sure is a magic flute
> Water walking boots
> plenty of food, including 2 tripe rations and 2 lizard corpses

I do not see either MR or reflection.  Either or both is crucial for you
at this point.

> Stormbringer (which I'm not using because I have no experience with
> longswords, plus I don't want to accidentally anger my pet arch-lich.
> I'm keeping it to either sell or enhance my score)

Eventually you may lose the pet.  At that point switch to it.  This is a
subject of much disagreement but to me this is one of the best artifact
weapons available.  Since Rodney gains a level every reincarnation it is
an extremely good idea to give him fewer and fewer levels across his
lives.  He falls sooner and sooner against Stormy.

> 6 teleportation scrolls of varying b/c/u status, plus several
> unidentified scrolls, and a blessed scroll of enchant armor which I'm
> saving for once I can get some GDSM (aka: the protection from YASD)
> 8 potions of holy water, a blessed potion of gain level (which I'm
> going to quaff once I level up normally to maximize its effect), A
> potion of booze, a potion of confusion, a potion of object detection,
> a potion of oil, and an unidentified potion
> 5 unidentified rings, +2 ring of gain constitution (being worn),
> cursed ring of searching, cursed ring of polymorph
> uncursed pickaxe
> 14 candles
> looking glass
> Blessed luckstone from gnomish mines (those work even if they're in
> your bag of holding, right?)

No.  The luckstone only works in open inventory.  Time to camp at an
altar and sac until you stop seeing clovers to ensure you are back to
max luck.

> Copious numbers of unidentified gems, a good number of which are
> probably valuable
> 13,059 zorkmids

Stash them.  You are now past much of their best uses.

> So here are my questions: First of all, do I have a descent chance of
> ascending?

Yes.

> Second, should I raid Fort Ludios before I do my quest or
> after?

First reflection then Ludios.  That only indirectly answers your
question but it does supply enough context.  If you need to do the Quest
to get reflection and/or MR first then do that.

